    "result_text": "Period numbering is in place and 3 of the 4 tests pass. The fourth, \"numbering per period scenario 3\", fails every time, and I think the spec contradicts itself at that step; it isn't something the numbering code causes.\n\n**What's wrong with scenario 3.** The step that fails (`acceptance.spec.ts:683`) edits Cam to grade C from 2026-04-02, while the sheet's today is 2026-03-20. The test helper only counts the edit as saved once Cam's row shows grade **C**. But the rest of the spec expects the opposite:\n- The expected audit line is `PERSON_EDITED \u2026 name=Cam grade=A`, not `grade=C`.\n- Later, with today at 2026-03-29, the spec expects Cam's grade to show **A**.\n\nThe row shows the grade in force on the sheet's today, which is still A until April 2. So the helper waits for a \"C\" that never appears and times out after 8 seconds. That part of the app is untouched by this change, and scenario 3 never opens a claim, so numbering plays no part in it. I can't edit the test, so I've left it as it is. If you know whether the edit should be refused or saved as A, I can change the app to match.\n\n**How the change works:**\n- **Setting:** the sheet has a new \"Period numbering from\" date in the Settings form, blank meaning off. Saving it writes `SETTING_CHANGED \u2026 key=period-numbering-from value=<date or empty>` to the audit file.\n- **Numbering:** while that date is set and the sheet's today is on or after it, opening a claim gives it the next number for the period its date falls in, like `P1-1`. A claim dated outside every period gets `X-<n>` from its own sequence. Otherwise the claim takes the next sheet-wide number. That sequence keeps counting while period numbering is on, so clearing the setting carries on where it left off (claims opened before it was set keep their numbers).\n- **Stored data:** a new migration, `V26__period_numbering.sql`, adds the setting to the sheet and a table holding each period's (and X's) last number, so numbers are never reused, even after a claim is voided. Claim numbers, and the number a correction refers to, are now stored as text so a correction can name `X-1`.\n- **Code touched:** on the server, `Claim`, `ClaimController`, `ClaimService` (the new `nextNumber`), a new `ClaimNumberSequence` entity and repository, `PeriodService.periodOn`, `Sheet`, and the settings controller and service. On the front end, the claims and settings services, `settings.ts`, and `person-claims.ts`, where the correction field now accepts numbers like `P1-1`.\n\nTwo side effects to know about:\n- A period named \"X\" shares its sequence with the claims that fall in no period. Numbers can't clash, but the two count together.\n- A claim's number keeps the period name it had when opened, even if the period is later renamed.",
